2026-09-23T07:05:46.1570088Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1570273Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1570505Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1570592Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1570700Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1570782Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1570880Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1570964Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1571074Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1571281Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1571383Z             return x + 1
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1571467Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1571549Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1571648Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1571749Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1571833Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1571909Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1572005Z     To execute it::
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1572089Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1572172Z         $ pytest
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1572341Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1572443Z         collected 1 items
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1572524Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1572627Z         test_sample.py F
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1572711Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1572862Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1573035Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1573119Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1573222Z             def test_answer():
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1573317Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1573422Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1573523Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1573605Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1573717Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1573881Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1573966Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1574043Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1574925Z     Thanks to ``pytest``'s detailed assertion introspection, you can simply use plain ``assert`` statements. See `getting-started <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/getting-started.html#our-first-test-run>`_ for more examples.
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1575016Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1575100Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1575183Z     Features
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1575274Z     --------
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1575357Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1575842Z     - Detailed info on failing `assert statements <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/assert.html>`_ (no need to remember ``self.assert*`` names)
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1576069Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1576174Z     - `Auto-discovery
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1576469Z       <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/goodpractices.html#python-test-discovery>`_
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1576577Z       of test modules and functions
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1576661Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1576933Z     - `Modular fixtures <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/fixtures.html>`_ for
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1577107Z       managing small or parametrized long-lived test resources
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1577192Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1577463Z     - Can run `unittest <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/unittest.html>`_ (or trial)
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1577562Z       test suites out of the box
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1577647Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1577747Z     - Python 3.10+ or PyPy3
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1577829Z     
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1578317Z     - Rich plugin architecture, with over 1300+ `external plugins <https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/plugin_list.html>`_ and thriving community
2026-09-23T07:05:46.1578404Z     
